## HTTP API

The pure ASGI middleware stores incoming `X-Trace-ID` in a request-local `ContextVar`.
Read it with `{{ package_name }}.trace.get_trace_id() -> str | None`.
Header names are case-insensitive. The first value is preserved as decoded by ASGI
(including an empty string); absent means `None`. No ID is generated or validated,
and no response header is added. The context resets in `finally` after normal,
failed or cancelled requests, and also covers mounted MCP in a combined application.
Do not treat unvalidated incoming trace IDs as trusted data when logging or displaying.


`GET /health` returns HTTP 200 with `{"status":"ok"}`. It is a liveness check,
not a database or external dependency readiness check. FastAPI exposes `/docs`.

```sh
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```
