## MCP

Transport: **{{ 'http' if use_http_api else mcp_transport }}**.
Tool `ping` takes an empty argument object `{}` and returns the string `pong`.
It performs no external actions. MCP clients initialize the connection, list tools,
then call `ping`; invalid arguments are reported as protocol/tool errors.
{% if use_http_api or mcp_transport == 'http' %}
Connect a Streamable HTTP MCP client to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp{{ '/' if use_http_api else '' }}`.
{% if use_http_api %}
The FastAPI lifespan starts and stops the mounted MCP service; `/mcp` may redirect to `/mcp/`.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
Configure the client to execute `uv run python -m {{ package_name }}` from this
project directory. Stdout is reserved for MCP protocol messages; logs use stderr.
Stop via the client's normal shutdown/EOF sequence.
{% endif %}
