### Explicit migrations

Review the environment and DATABASE_URL before each command. Import application
models in `migrations/env.py` when you add them so autogenerate can see their metadata.

```sh
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
uv run --locked ruff check --select I --fix migrations
just format-src
uv run --locked ruff check migrations
uv run --locked ruff format --check migrations
# Review the generated revision; agree on any missing transformation before applying it.
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

After generating or editing a revision, sort its imports and run `just format-src`
as shown above before checks or applying it. Alembic emits Python source that may
need formatting, including quote normalization. Inspect these mechanical changes
and the migration operations; formatting does not establish migration correctness.

Migrations use the selected async driver and run only on explicit command. Offline
mode is unsupported. Never call `create_all` as a substitute for migration history.
{% if database == 'sqlite' %}
SQLite migrations enable batch rendering for table alterations; review generated
batch operations, database file location and backup requirements before applying.
