## Configuration and resources

{% if use_settings %}
`Settings` uses typed pydantic-settings environment fields. No `.env` is loaded
implicitly; invalid values raise validation errors with input values hidden.
{% else %}
`Settings` reads environment variables using the standard library; pydantic-settings
is not a direct runtime dependency. No `.env` loader is used.
{% endif %}
{% if use_http_client %}
The lifespan opens an `httpx.AsyncClient` with a 10-second timeout and closes it
on shutdown, including failure paths. `resources()` yields it as `state["http_client"]`.
{% endif %}
`{{ package_name }}.resources.resources()` is an async context manager yielding the
selected resource dictionary. Do not hold SQL transactions during external requests.
Application logs use standard `logging`; do not log credentials or DATABASE_URL.
{% if use_mcp %}
The MCP lifespan owns resources; retrieve its state via FastMCP's lifespan context.
{% elif use_http_api %}
HTTP handlers can access lifespan resources through `request.app.state.resources`.
{% endif %}

## Checks

```sh
just precommit-check-agent
```

pytest supports async tests; Ruff excludes tests but checks application and migration
Python. Bandit and pip-audit are included. HTTPX is also a development dependency for
transport checks, independently of the optional runtime client. No CI, Docker,
authentication, deployment, or automatic migrations are configured.

The original template MIT notice is retained in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` in generated
projects, including when the project license is `none`. This does not license newly
added project code automatically.
